  "Case File: Nurse Murder and Arson ": "",
  "The phone numbers Shintani contacted on the day of his murder, conveniently left in his call history. The last call he ever made turned out to be to the Advanced Drug Development Center.": "",
  "AD-9 was released by the Advanced Drug Development Center in 2017 after showing miraculous results on the previously-incurable Alzheimer's disease. Kido may be credited as lead author, but Prof. Youji Shono did all the actual research; they just slapped a big-shot pharma bro's name on the cover as a publicity stunt.": "",
  "A freelance journalist. While other \"reporters\" are reposting clickbait, he's still hitting the pavement in search of the next big story.": "",
  "Gengoro Miki": "",
  "A pro wrestler turned public servant. He used to play the villain, but had a heel-face turn and became a politician of justice by showing his true face in public; polls say voters preferred the mask.": "",
  "Wiretap": "",
  "A wiretap from Tsukumo. It's made to be plugged discreetly into an electrical outlet.": "",
  "Ruan Wang": "",
  "The client. An executive member of what he calls \"the organization.\" It seems the boss of the organization took care of him and to return that kindness, he wants to take in Zhuang Shi.": "",
  "A man from the organization that's been targeting Zhuang Shi. When Wang said \"executive member,\" he probably meant this guy. If I try to take the cat, it's safe to say he'll interfere.": "",
  "Zhuang Shi": "",
  "This Diamond Eye cat is a rare breed worth a grand fortune; it's also being targeted by a shadowy organization. Now that's what I call an aristocat.": "",
  "Photo of Zhuang Shi": "",
  "A photo of the client's missing cat. His white fur and grand collar stick out like a sore paw.": "",
  "Cat Food": "",
  "A can of cat food, compliments of the cat café's owner.": "",
  "Shizue Kuwayama": "",
  "The client. She got it in her head that Kiriko might one day murder her son.": "",
  "Kojiro's wife. Shizue doesn't seem to think too highly of her.": "",
  "Kojiro Kuwayama": "",
  "Shizue's son. He's apparently \"head over heels\" for Kiriko; haven't heard that cliche in a while.": "",
  "Photo of Kojiro and Kiriko": "",
  "A photo of Kiriko and her husband, Kojiro.": "",
  "Suspicious Powder": "",
  "A garlicky substance left on the rim of Kojiro's coffee cup. Possibly poison.": "",
  "Takeshi Akagawa": "",
  "A young man whose jacket was stolen. Apparently the jacket's worth more than his life... so why'd he leave it in a bathroom? I can solve the case, but I can't fix stupid.": "",
  "Akagawa's Missing Property": "",
  "A list of Akagawa's lost belongings. Inside the yellow duffle was a blue-and-white jacket with an embroidered tiger, a blue cloth wallet, and a yellow wristwatch.": "",
  "Warm Clothes": "",
  "Clothes that are warm enough to survive a night under the cold night sky.": "",
  "Used Accessory": "",
  "One of the burglars is getting particular about their fashion. They've been dressing head to toe in name brand items, clearly sending the message that they're not lacking in money.": "",
  "Oathbreaker Crow": "",
  "Crow broke the burglary ring's rule to steal only from the corrupt in order to stuff his own pockets. Jester drew a line in the sand and left the ring rather than work with Crow.": "",
  "Panties": "",
  "Undergarments with the same design as the ones Tsukino usually wears. I'll be in deep shit if the police check my belongings right now. I better hurry up, keep my head low, and hang it on the roof to lure out the pervert.": "",
  "Photo of Takefumi Hashimoto": "",
  "A photo of Takefumi Hashimoto. Right now, it's my only lead on finding the target.": "",
  "Photo of Taro Iseya": "",
  "A photo of Taro Iseya, the sexually harassing boss. Better keep an eye on this dirtbag.": "",
  "Some old work clothes. Used to inflitrate the scene.": "",
  "Sana's CD": "",
  "A CD with Sana-chan's songs on it. Maybe it'll be a collector's item one day?": "",
  "Saito's Business Card": "",
  "Business card from Saito. It says \"Super Cinderella Productions Co., Ltd. Producer Haruaki Saito. Taihei Boulevard East, Ishiyama Building, 4th Floor. Tel: 03-5555-4649\".": "",
  "Photo of Hideaki Deguchi": "",
  "A photo of Hideaki Deguchi, Taniyama-san's nephew.": "",
  "Photo of Yukako": "",
  "A photo of Shimazu-san's pride and joy: his girlfriend.": "",
  "Bram Sylvania's nocturnal vestments. I am so not looking forward to wearing this.": "",
  "Tabloid Magazine": "",
  "Includes a gossip article exposing Hinata's scandalous night of passion with a minor.": "",
  "Photo of Hachitani": "",
  "A photo of the blonde woman with a mole who allegedly honey-trapped Hinata.": "",
  "Chatter Screen": "",
  "The Chatter screen displaying Hachitani's recent posts. 20 min ago: Shopped at Don Quijote. 10 min ago: Saw a movie trailer by a ramen shop. 8 min ago: Walked close to a sex store. 5 min ago: Stood near a beef bowl shop. 1 min ago: Ate an onion ring.": "",
  "Tsukino's twin brother. He may look just like his beloved \"younger\" sister, but he's got a mischievous streak to him.": "",
  "Yosuke's twin sister. She looks just like her \"older\" brother. Panty Professor stole her favorite undergarments (black lace lingerie with a ribbon).": "",
  "A sex criminal who only steals female lingerie. This underwear thief from the Twisted Trio used a drone to snatch Tsukino's panties.": "",
  "Yosuke's twin sister. She looks just like her \"older\" brother. She was victimized by the Twisted Trio.": "",
  "A sex criminal who gropes his victims' rear ends. This handsy hooligan from the Twisted Trio managed to cop a feel of Tsukino's butt.": "",
  "Yosuke's twin sister. She looks just like her \"older\" brother. Hasn't left the house since Judge Creep 'n Peep photographed her naked with her boyfriend.": "",
  "A sex criminal who posts photos of \"guilty\" people having sex. This peeping pervert from the Twisted Trio spied on Tsukino during intercourse.": "",
  "Yosuke's twin sister. She looks just like her \"older\" brother. She saw Giant Impact's rocket ship... Hope she knows that's not normal.": "",
  "Giant Impact": "",
  "The Pervert King, named after a theory about the formation of the moon. I wonder if his rocket ship lives up to the astronomical title, but I'm afraid to find out.": "",
  "An unidentified terrorist who set up explosives in Kamurocho. Their motives are unknown.": "",
  "Tomokazu Kawada": "",
  "An editor at Cloudy Skies Publishing. He requested that I solve some kind of riddle. The reward is publishing rights to a new novel by award-winning mystery writer Takumi Katagiri.": "",
  "Japan's greatest mystery novelist, famous for his \"Edison\" series. He's posing some sort of puzzle, and will reward the first one to solve it with the rights to publish his newest book.": "",
  "Noriko Taguchi": "",
  "A woman who runs Heavy Coffee, the café on Taihei Blvd. She suspects her husband's recent uptick in going out is a sign of infidelity.": "",
  "Masayoshi Taguchi": "",
  "A man who helps his wife run Heavy Coffee, the café on Taihei Blvd. He's been leaving the house more for the last six months; Noriko thinks he's cheating on her.": "",
  "Megumi Hashimoto": "",
  "A client who suspects her husband of infidelity. Seems like a caring housewife.": "",
  "Takefumi Hashimoto": "",
  "Megumi's husband. The CEO of a real estate agency should have plenty of cash to blow on an illicit affair...": "",
  "A young professional being sexually harassed by her boss. It's clear from the office's toxic culture that any reports she files will either be ignored or result in retaliation.": "",
  "Taro Iseya": "",
  "A sorry excuse for a corporate drone; flexes his CEO daddy's influence to sexually harass Rei with impunity.": "",
  "A girl who dreams of being a singer-songwriter. The streets have been her only stage, but she already has a loyal fanbase. Maybe I should ask for her autograph now.": "",
  "Fumie Taniyama": "",
  "A kindhearted aunt who loaned ¥500,000 to her nephew, Deguchi. Her daughter is getting married soon, so she needs a large sum of cash, fast.": "",
  "Taniyama-san's nephew who came to Tokyo to become a host. Both his parents passed away. His aunt hasn't heard from him in a while and is worried that he's lost sight of his dreams.": "",
  "A man whose female employee went missing. He went to Yagami for help because Mami had a stalker.": "",
  "A woman who was being by harassed a stalker for an extended period of time went missing.": "",
  "A misfortune teller who predicts nothing but doom. Her ill omens always come true, but those who expect trouble are never surprised.": "",
  "A man terrified of a \"black\" calamity. He has horrible luck, which only seems to get worse each time he visits Amane.": "",
  "A misfortune teller who sees imminent disaster as shadows. Her predictions are never wrong, but with preparation the worst can be evaded.": "",
  "A man who lives in fear of a \"black and white\" calamity. Some folks just have all the bad luck.": "",
  "Another man Amane-san saw a calamity associated with. When she warned him of a fiery disaster in his future, he struck her and immediately stormed off.": "",
  "Mamoru Shimazu": "",
  "The client. He has plans to move in with his long-distance girlfriend.": "",
  "Yukako Oki": "",
  "The client. Her boyfriend Shimazu is missing, so she's come to me for help finding him.": "",
  "Yukako Oki's boyfriend. According to my client, he's gone missing.": "",
  "Toya Tokunaga": "",
  "A hot young idol on the fast track to fame. Most celebrities have their quirks, but this one's personality changes whenever he puts on a wig.": "",
  "The leader of a burglary ring targeting Kamurocho. His name and age are unknown. Like his pseudonym suggests, he wears a black bird mask.": "",
  "Jester": "",
  "The wild card of the burglary ring targeting Kamurocho. His name and age are unknown. He first used Yagami to escape the police, but then saved him from the Matsugane Family. His actions are shrouded in mystery. Cannot be contacted.": "",
  "A regular at Tender. Her name, age, and occupation are unknown, yet everyone tells her everything, as if they've known her a long time. She's a mysterious woman like that.": "",
  "Yusuke": "",
  "A young boy who Kaito saved from danger. He sees Kaito as a hero of justice and looks up to him with passionate admiration in his pure, innocent eyes. Yusuke has finally met his hero.": "",
  "Apparently saved Yusuke from thugs. He's rough around the edges but can't ignore a helpless person in need, so it's no surprise that some see him as a hero of justice.": "",
  "Shunei Oikawa": "",
  "A student of Genda. He was once a skilled lawyer who would do anything to win a trial. One day he went too far and was fired from the law firm.": "",
  "Azusa Otaki": "",
  "Genda's client. She's battling her husband for custody over their daughter, Karin.": "",
  "Karin Otaki": "",
  "Azusa's daughter. She's caught up in a custody battle between her divorcing parents.": "",
  "Jin Otaki": "",
  "Azusa's husband, former yakuza. He quit his life of crime and now works as a civilian.": "",
  "Makihara": "",
  "A man who loves drones. He lost control of a prototype's test flight and hit me. As an apology, he tuned up my drone to be raceable.": "",
  "Disabled Veteran": "",
  "The homeless man with a limp who gave me a VR play pass. He said he'll lead me to Red Nose in exchange for the grand prize from Dice & Cube.": "",
  "Hajime Obayashi": "",
  "A bounty hunter after the price on my head. No way am I getting caught by the likes of him!": "",
  "A pilot who got called in on his wife's birthday. He was on standby, but if he wore his uniform to a restaurant, he had to have expected this? I may never know the answer.": "",
  "Naoko": "",
  "Tatsuro's wife. She's plastered, so I guess I'm her husband now. You don't need to be a private eye to deduce that she's thirsty for more than just booze.": "",
  "Hayato Adachi": "",
  "Kaito-san's best friend since childhood. He was an honor-roll kid, but he'd still sneak out and raise hell with Kaito.": ""
 },
